5 -65\u221a14/56)y.\n\nConvert to common denominator: 56/56 -65/56 = (-9/56)y\u221a14.\n\nConstants: -11 -39 = -50.\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\n(-3/10)x - (9\u221a14/56)y -50 = 0.\n\nMultiply both sides by 280 (the least common multiple of denominators 10, 56) to eliminate fractions:\n\n(-3/10)x *280 = -84x.\n\n(-9\u221a14/56)y *280 = -45\u221a14 y.\n\n-50 *280 = -14000.\n\nSo, equation becomes:\n\n-84x -45\u221a14 y -14000 = 0.\n\nBring constants to the other side:\n\n-84x -45\u221a14 y = 14000.\n\nDivide both sides by -3 to simplify:\n\n28x +15\u221a14 y = -14000/3.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Maybe I made a mistake in the calculation.\n\nWait, let me double-check the combining of terms.\n\nFrom the tangent at C:\n\nFirst term: 22/5 x.\n\nSecond term: 12\u221a14/5 y.\n\nThird term: -5/2 x.\n\nFourth term: -65\u221a14/56 y.\n\nFifth term: -11.\n\nSixth term: -39.\n\nSo, combining x terms: 22/5 x -5/2 x.\n\nCompute 22/5 -5/2 = (44/10 -25/10) = 19/10.\n\nSo, x term is (19/10)x.\n\nSimilarly, y terms: 12\u221a14/5 y -65\u221a14/56 y.\n\nCompute 12\u221a14/5 -65\u221a14/56.\n\nConvert to common denominator: 56/56 -65/56 = (-53/56)\u221a14.\n\nWait, 12*56=672, 5*56=280.\n\nWait, 12/5 is 2.4, 65/56 is approximately 1.16.\n\nWait, let me compute 12/5 -65/56.\n\nCompute 12/5 = 2.4, 65/56 \u22481.16, so 2.4 -1.16\u22481.24.\n\nBut let's compute exactly:\n\n12/5 -65/56 = (12*56 -65*5)/(5*56) = (672 - 325)/280 = 347/280.\n\nSo, y term is (347/280)\u221a14 y.\n\nWait, that's positive. Hmm, because 12/5 -65/56 = positive.\n\nWait, but in the equation, it's (12\u221a14/5 -65\u221a14/56)y, which is (12/5 -65/56)\u221a14 y.\n\nSo, 12/5 -65/56 = (12*56 -65*5)/(5*56) = (672 - 325)/280 = 347/280.\n\nSo, y term is 347\u221a14/280 y.\n\nConstants: -11 -39 = -50.\n\nSo, overall equation is:\n\n(19/10)x + (347\u221a14/280)y -50 = 0.\n\nMultiply both sides by 280 to eliminate denominators:\n\n(19/10)x *280 = 532x.\n\n(347\u221a14/280)y *280 = 347\u221a14 y.\n\n-50 *280 = -14000.