4 /5 +347\u221a14)y +532=14,000.\n\nConvert 347\u221a14 to fifths:\n\n347\u221a14= (347*5\u221a14)/5= (1735\u221a14)/5.\n\nThus, total y term:\n\n(247\u221a14 +1735\u221a14)/5= (1982\u221a14)/5.\n\nThus, equation:\n\n(1982\u221a14 /5)y +532=14,000.\n\nSubtract 532:\n\n(1982\u221a14 /5)y=14,000 -532=13,468.\n\nThus, y=13,468 *5 / (1982\u221a14)= (67,340)/(1982\u221a14).\n\nSimplify numerator and denominator:\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 2:\n\n67,340 \u00f72=33,670.\n\n1982 \u00f72=991.\n\nThus, y=33,670 / (991\u221a14).\n\nSimplify 33,670 and 991:\n\nCheck if 991 divides 33,670.\n\n33,670 \u00f7991= approx 33,670 \u00f71000\u224833.67, so 33,670=991*33 + remainder.\n\nCompute 991*33=32,743.\n\n33,670 -32,743=927.\n\nThus, 33,670=991*33 +927.\n\nThus, y=(991*33 +927)/(991\u221a14)= [991*33 +927]/(991\u221a14).\n\nFactor numerator:\n\n991*33 +927=991*33 +927.\n\nNot sure if it factors further. Alternatively, perhaps 991 is a prime? Let me check.\n\n991: Let's see, square root is about 31.5. Check primes up to 31.\n\n991 \u00f72: No.\n\n991 \u00f73: 9+9+1=19, not divisible by 3.\n\n991 \u00f75: Ends with 1, no.\n\n7: 7*141=987, 987+4=991, so no.\n\n11: 9 -9 +1=1, not divisible by 11.\n\n13: 13*76=988, 988+3=991, not divisible.\n\n17: 17*58=986, 986+5=991, not divisible.\n\n19: 19*52=988, 988+3=991, not divisible.\n\n23: 23*43=989, 989+2=991, not divisible.\n\n29: 29*34=986, 986+5=991, not divisible.\n\n31: 31*31=961, 31*32=992, which is over. So 991 is prime.\n\nThus, y= (33*991 +927)/(991\u221a14)= (33*991 +927)/(991\u221a14).\n\nNot sure if we can factor numerator more.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps we can compute it numerically, but maybe we can keep it symbolic.\n\nSimilarly, x= [13\u221a14 y +140]/140.\n\nWe can substitute y= (33,670)/(991\u221a14).\n\nThus, x= [13\u221a14*(33,670)/(991\u221a14) +140]/140.\n\nSimplify:\n\n\u221a14 cancels:\n\nx= [13*33,670 /991 +140]/140.\n\nCompute 13*33,670=438,710.\n\nThus, x= (438,710 /991 +140)/140.\n\nCompute 438,710 \u