 coordinates:\n\nA(0,0), B(5,0), C(22/5, 12\u221a14 /5).\n\nNow, tangents from D to circle \u03c9 at points B and C.\n\nPoint D is the ex-tangent point.\n\nWe can compute coordinates of D.\n\nFirst, since D is the intersection of tangents at B and C.\n\nThe tangent at B: since \u03c9 is the circumcircle of ABC.\n\nFirst, compute equation of tangent at B.\n\nThe tangent at point B can be found using the formula for tangent to a circle at a point.\n\nBut first, we need the center of \u03c9.\n\nCompute center of \u03c9: since it's the circumcircle of ABC.\n\nCoordinates of A(0,0), B(5,0), C(22/5,12\u221a14 /5).\n\nTo find the circumcircle, we can compute perpendicular bisectors of AB and AC.\n\nMidpoint of AB: (2.5,0). Slope of AB: (0-0)/(5-0)=0, so perpendicular bisector is vertical line x=2.5.\n\nMidpoint of AC: (11/5,6\u221a14 /5). Compute slope of AC: (12\u221a14 /5 -0)/(22/5 -0)= (12\u221a14 /5)/(22/5)=12\u221a14 /22=6\u221a14 /11.\n\nThus, slope of perpendicular bisector is negative reciprocal: -11/(6\u221a14).\n\nEquation of perpendicular bisector of AC: passing through midpoint (11/5,6\u221a14 /5).\n\nPoint-slope form: y -6\u221a14 /5= (-11)/(6\u221a14)(x -11/5).\n\nNow, find intersection with x=2.5=5/2.\n\nSubstitute x=5/2 into equation:\n\ny -6\u221a14 /5= (-11)/(6\u221a14)(5/2 -11/5).\n\nCompute 5/2 -11/5= (25/10 -22/10)=3/10.\n\nThus, y=6\u221a14 /5 + (-11)/(6\u221a14)*(3/10).\n\nSimplify:\n\ny=6\u221a14 /5 - (33)/(60\u221a14)=6\u221a14 /5 - 11/(20\u221a14).\n\nRationalize the second term: 11/(20\u221a14)=11\u221a14 / (20*14)=11\u221a14 /280.\n\nThus, y=6\u221a14 /5 -11\u221a14 /280.\n\nConvert to common denominator:\n\n6\u221a14 /5= (6\u221a14 *56)/280=336\u221a14 /280.\n\nThus, y=336\u221a14 /280 -11\u221a14 /280=325\u221a14 /280=65\u221a14 /56.\n\nThus, center of \u03c9 is at (5/2,65\u221a14 /56).\n\nCompute radius: distance from center to A(0,0):\n\n\u221a[(5/2)^2 + (65\u221a14 /56)^2].\n\nCompute (5/2)^2=25/4.\n\nCompute (65\u221a14 /56)^2=(65^2 *14)/(56^2)= (4225*14)/(3136)=59,190 /3136.\n\nSimplify 59,190 \u00f714=4,235. 3136 \u00f714=224.\n\nThus, 4,235 /224. 4,235 \u00f77=605, 224 \u00f77=32. So, 605 /32.\n\nThus, radius squared is 25/4 + 605/32= (200/32 +605/32)=805/32.\n\nThus, radius is sqrt(805/32)=sqrt(805)/ (4\u221a2).\n\nBut maybe not needed.\n\nNow, equation of tangent at B(5,0).\n\nThe tangent at point B on circle with center (h,k) is (x -h)(x1 -h) + (y -k)(y1 -k)=r\u00b2.\n\nWait, no, the equation is (x1 -h)(x -h) + (y1 -k)(y -k)=r\u00b2.\n\nWait, actually, the tangent at point (x1,y1) on circle with center (h,k) is (x1 -h)(x -h) + (y1 -k)(y -k)=r\u00b2.\n\nWait, no, that's not correct. The correct equation is (x1 -h)(x -h) + (y1 -k)(y -k)=r\u00b2.\n\nBut actually, the tangent line is perpendicular to the radius, so the slope is - (x1 -h)/(y1 -k).\n\nThus, equation is y - y1= m(x -x1), where m= - (x1 -h)/(y1 -k).\n\nSo, for point B(5,0), center is (5/2,65\u221a14 /56).\n\nThus, slope m= - (5 -5/2)/(0 -65\u221a14 /56)= - (5/2)/(-65\u221a14 /56)= (5/2)/(65\u221a14 /56)= (5/2)*(56)/(65\u221a14)= (5*28)/(65\u221a14)=140/(65\u221a14)=28/(13\u221a14).\n\nRationalize: 28/(13\u221a14)=28\u221a14/(13*14)=2\u221a14 /13.\n\nThus, equation of tangent at B: y -0= (2\u221a14 /13)(x -5).\n\nSo, y= (2\u221a14 /13)x -10\u221a14 /13.\n\nSimilarly, tangent at C(22/5,12\u221a14 /5).\n\nCompute slope of radius OC: from center (5/2,65\u221a14 /56) to C(22/5,12\u221a14 /5).\n\nCompute slope: (12\u221a14 /5 -65\u221a14 /56)/(22/5 -5/2).\n\nFirst, numerator:\n\n12\u221a14 /5 -65\u221a14 /56= (12*56\u221a14 -65*5\u221a14)/280= (672\u221a14 -325\u221a14)/280=347\u221a14 /280.\n\nDenominator:\n\n22/5 -5/2= (44 -25)/10=19/10.\n\nThus, slope of radius is (347\u221a14 /280)/(19/10)= (347\u221a14 /280)*(10/19)= (347\u221a14 *10)/(280*19)= (3470\u221a14)/(5320)= Simplify.\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 10: 347\u221a14 /532.\n\nSimplify 347 and 532: 347 is prime? 347 \u00f713=26.69, not integer. 347 \u00f77=49.57, no. 347 \u00f717=20.41, no. So, 347 is prime.\n\nThus, slope m= (347\u221a14)/532.\n\nThus, slope of tangent is negative reciprocal: m_tangent= -532/(347\u221a14)= -532\u221a14/(347*14)= -532\u221a14 /4828.\n\nSimplify 532 \u00f714=38, so 532=14*38.\n\nThus, m_tangent= - (14*38)\u221a14 / (347*14)= -38\u221a14 /347.\n\nThus, equation of tangent at C: y -12\u221a14 /5= (-38\u221a14 /347)(x -22/5).\n\nNow, we have two tangent lines:\n\n1. Tangent at B: y= (2\u221a14 /13)x -10\u221a14 /13.\n\n2. Tangent at C: y -12\u221a14 /5= (-38\u221a14 /347)(x -22/5).\n\nWe can find their intersection point D.\n\nSo, solve the two equations:\n\nEquation 1: y= (2\u221a14 /13)x -10\u221a14 /13.\n\nEquation 2: y= (-38\u221a14 /347)x + (38\u221a14 /347)*(22/5) +12\u221a14 /5.\n\nLet me compute equation 2:\n\nFirst, expand:\n\ny= (-38\u221a14 /347)x + (38\u221a14 /347)*(22/5) +12\u221a14 /5.\n\nCompute constants:\n\n(38\u221a14 /347)*(22/5)= (836\u221a14)/1715.\n\n12\u221a14 /5= (714\u221a14)/1715.\n\nThus, adding constants: (836\u221a14 +714\u221a14)/1715= (1550\u221a14)/1715= (310\u221a14)/343.\n\nThus, equation 2: y= (-38\u221a14 /347)x +310\u221a14 /343.\n\nNow, set equation 1 equal to equation 2:\n\n(2\u221a14 /13)x -10\u221a14 /13 = (-38\u221a14 /347)x +310\u221a14 /343.\n\nDivide both sides by \u221a14 to simplify:\n\n2/13 x -10/13 = (-38 /347)x +310 /343.\n\nMultiply both sides by 13*347*343 to eliminate denominators.\n\nCompute LCM of denominators 13,347,343.\n\n13 is prime. 347: check if prime. 347 \u00f713=26.69, not integer. 347 \u00f77=49.57, no. 347 \u00f73=115.666, no. So, 347 is prime. 343=7^3.\n\nThus, LCM is 13*347*343.\n\nMultiply both sides by 13*347*343:\n\n2*347*343 x -10*347*343 = (-38*13*343)x +310*13*347.\n\nCompute each term:\n\nFirst term: 2*347*343 x=2*347*343 x.\n\nSecond term: -10*347*343.\n\nThird term: -38*13*343 x.\n\nFourth term: 310*13*347.\n\nLet me compute each coefficient:\n\nCompute 2*347*343: 2*347=694; 694*343. Let's compute 694*300=208,200; 694*43=29,842. So total 208,200 +29,842=238,042. So, first term:238,042 x.\n\nSecond term: -10*347*343= -10*347= -3,470; -3,470*343. Compute 3,470*300=1,041,000; 3,470*43=149, 410? Wait, 3,470*40=138,800; 3,470*3=10,410. So total 138,800 +10,410=149,210. Thus, total second term: -1,041,000 -149,210= -1,190,210.\n\nThird term: -38*13*343= -38*13= -494; -494*343. Compute 494*300=148,200; 494*43=21,202. So total 148,200 +21,202=169,402. Thus, third term: -169,402 x.\n\nFourth term: 310*13*347=310*13=4,030; 4,030*347. Compute 4,000*347=1,388,000; 30*347=10,410. So total 1,388,000 +10,410=1,398,410.\n\nThus, equation becomes:\n\n238,042 x -1,190,210 = -169,402 x +1,398,410.\n\nBring all terms to left side:\n\n238,042 x +169,402 x -1,190,210 -1,398,410=0.\n\nCompute 238,042 +169,402=407,444.\n\nThus, 407,444 x -2,588,620=0.\n\nThus, 407,444 x=2,588,620.\n\nThus, x=2,588,620 /407,444.\n\nSimplify fraction:\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 4: 2,588,620 \u00f74=647,155; 407,444 \u00f74=101,861.\n\nCheck if 101,861 divides 647,155.\n\nCompute 101,861*6=611,266; 647,155 -611,266=35,889.\n\n101,861*0.35\u224835, 889? 101,861*0.35\u224835,  101,861*0.3=30,558.3; 101,861*0.05\u22485,093.05; total\u224835,651.35. Close to 35,889.\n\nSo, approximately 6.35 times. Not exact. So, maybe no common factors. Let me check GCD(647,155,101,861).\n\nCompute GCD(101,861,647,155). Compute 647,155 \u00f7101,861=6 with remainder 647,155 -6*101,861=647,155 -611,266=35,889.\n\nNow compute GCD(101,861,35,889). 101,861 \u00f735,889=2 with remainder 101,861 -2*35,889=101,861 -71,778=30,083.\n\nGCD(35,889,30,083). 35,889 \u00f730,083=1 with remainder 35,889 -30,083=5,806.\n\nGCD(30,083,5,806). 30,083 \u00f75,806=5 with remainder 30,083 -5*5,806=30,083 -29,030=1,053.\n\nGCD(5,806,1,053). 5,806 \u00f71,053=5 with remainder 5,806 -5*1,053=5,806 -5,265=541.\n\nGCD(1,053,541). 1,053 \u00f7541=1 with remainder 512.\n\nGCD(541,512). 541 \u00f7512=1 with remainder 29.\n\nGCD(512,29). 512 \u00f729=17 with remainder 512 -17*29=512 -493=19.\n\nGCD(29,19). 29 \u00f719=1 with remainder 10.\n\nGCD(19,10). 19 \u00f710=1 with remainder 9.\n\nGCD(10,9). 10 \u00f79=1 with remainder 1.\n\nGCD(9,1)=1.\n\nThus, GCD is 1. So, fraction is reduced.\n\nThus, x=2,588,620 /407,444= (2,588,620 \u00f74)/(407,444 \u00f74)=647,155 /101,861.\n\nWait, no, 2,588,620 \u00f74=647,155, and 407,444 \u00f74=101,861.\n\nThus, x=647,155 /101,861.\n\nSo, x=647,155 /101,861. Simplify further? Since GCD is 1, it's already in lowest terms.\n\nNow, compute y from equation 1: y=(2\u221a14 /13)x - (2\u221a14)/13.\n\nWait, equation 1: y= (2\u221a14 /13)x - (2\u221a14)/13.\n\nSo, y= (2\u221a14 /13)*(647,155 /101,861) - (2\u221a14)/13.\n\nFactor out (2\u221a14)/13:\n\ny= (2\u221a14)/13*(647,155 /101,861 -1)= (2\u221a14)/13*(647,155 -101,861)/101,861= (2\u221a14)/13*(545,294 /101,861).\n\nSimplify 545,294 /101,861.\n\nCompute 101,861*5=509,305. 545,294 -509,305=35,989.\n\n101,861*0.35\u224835, 989? 101,861*0.35\u224835, 989? Let's see: 101,861*0.3=30,558.3; 101,861*0.05=5,093.05; total\u224835,651.35. Close to 35,989.\n\nSo, approximately 5.35.\n\nBut exact value: 35,989 \u00f7101,861\u22480.3535.\n\nThus, 545,294 /101,861=5 +35,989 /101,861=5 + (approx 0.3535)=5.3535.\n\nBut exact fraction: 35,989 and101,861.\n\nCheck GCD(35,989,101,861).\n\nCompute 101,861 \u00f735,989=2 with remainder 101,861 -2*35,989=101,861 -71,978=29,883.\n\nGCD(35,989,29,883). 35,989 \u00f729,883=1 with remainder 6,106.\n\nGCD(29,883,6,106). 29,883 \u00f76,106=4 with remainder 29,883 -4*6,106=29,883 -24,424=5,459.\n\nGCD(6,106,5,459). 6,106 \u00f75,459=1 with remainder 647.\n\nGCD(5,459,647). 5,459 \u00f7647=8 with remainder 5,459 -8*647=5,459 -5,176=283.\n\nGCD(647,283). 647 \u00f7283=2 with remainder 647 -2*283=647 -566=81.\n\nGCD(283,81). 283 \u00f781=3 with remainder 283 -3*81=283 -243=40.\n\nGCD(81,40). 81 \u00f740=2 with remainder 1.\n\nGCD(40,1)=1.\n\nThus, GCD is 1. So, 35,989 /101,861 is reduced.\n\nThus, 545,294 /101,861=5 +35,989 /101,861=5 + (35,989 /101,861).\n\nThus, y= (2\u221a14)/13*(5 +35,989 /101,861)= (2\u221a14)/13*(5 +35,989 /101,861).\n\nThis is getting complicated. Maybe instead of trying to compute it directly, we can use another approach.\n\nWait, maybe use inversion or projective geometry? Or maybe use power of a point.\n\nWait, point D is the ex-tangent point, so power of D with respect to \u03c9 is DB\u00b2=DC\u00b2=DA*DP, since AD meets \u03c9 again at P.\n\nThus, power of D: DB\u00b2=DA*DP.\n\nThus, DP= DB\u00b2 / DA.\n\nSo, if we can compute DB and DA, then compute DP.\n\nThus, let's compute DB and DA.\n\nFirst, coordinates of D: complicated, but maybe we can compute distances DA and DB.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use coordinates.\n\nWait, let me try to compute coordinates of D.\n\nFrom earlier, we have point D=(x,y)= (647,155 /101,861, (2\u221a14)/13*(647,155 /101,861) - (2\u221a14)/13).\n\nBut this is messy.\n\nAlternatively, since D is the ex-tangent point, maybe we can compute it using triangle centers.\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to compute coordinates of D as the intersection of tangents at B and C.\n\nGiven points B=(5,0) and C=(22/5,12\u221a14 /5).\n\nWe can find equations of tangents at B and C, then find their intersection D.\n\nEquation of tangent at B: since B is (5,0), and \u03c9 is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + Dx + Ey + F=0.\n\nWait, but we have \u03c9 as x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 -5x - (65\u221a14 /28)y - something=0.\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to write the equation of \u03c9.\n\nWait, earlier, we had point A=(0,0), B=(5,0), C=(22/5,12\u221a14 /5).\n\nThus, the circumcircle passes through A, B, C.\n\nThus, equation of circle is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + Dx + Ey + F=0.\n\nSince it passes through A(0,0): 0 +0 +0 +0 + F=0 => F=0.\n\nSo, equation is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + Dx + Ey=0.\n\nPasses through B(5,0): 25 +0 +5D +0=0 =>5D= -25 => D= -5.\n\nPasses through C(22/5,12\u221a14 /5): (22/5)^2 + (12\u221a14 /5)^2 + (-5)(22/5) + E*(12\u221a14 /5)=0.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n(22/5)^2=484/25.\n\n(12\u221a14 /5)^2= (144*14)/25=2016/25.\n\n-5*(22/5)= -22.\n\nE*(12\u221a14 /5)= (12\u221a14 E)/5.\n\nThus, equation:\n\n484/25 + 2016/25 -22 + (12\u221a14 E)/5=0.\n\nCompute 484 +2016=2500, so 2500/25=100.\n\nThus, 100 -22 + (12\u221a14 E)/5=0 =>78 + (12\u221a14 E)/5=0.\n\nThus, (12\u221a14 E)/5= -78 => E= (-78 *5)/(12\u221a14)= (-390)/(12\u221a14)= (-65)/(2\u221a14).\n\nRationalize denominator: (-65)/(2\u221a14)*(\u221a14/\u221a14)= (-65\u221a14)/28.\n\nThus, equation of circle is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 -5x + Ey=0, with E= -65\u221a14 /28.\n\nThus, equation: x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 -5x - (65\u221a14 /28)y=0.\n\nThus, tangent at B(5,0): formula for tangent at (x1,y1) on circle x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 +Dx + Ey + F=0 is xx1 + yy1 + D(x +x1)/2 + E(y + y1)/2 + F=0.\n\nBut here, F=0, D=-5, E= -65\u221a14 /28.\n\nThus, tangent at B(5,0): x*5 + y*0 + (-5)(x +5)/2 + (-65\u221a14 /28)(y +0)/2=0.\n\nSimplify:\n\n5x - (5)(x +5)/2 - (65\u221a14 /28)(y)/2=0.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n5x - (5x +25)/2 - (65\u221a14 y)/56=0.\n\nMultiply all terms by 56 to eliminate denominators:\n\n56*5x -56*(5x +25)/2 -56*(65\u221a14 y)/56=0.\n\nSimplify:\n\n280x -140*(5x +25)/2 -65\u221a14 y=0.\n\nWait, 56*(5x +25)/2=28*(5x +25)=140x +3500.\n\nWait, no:\n\nWait, 56*(5x +25)/2=28*(5x +25)=140x +700.\n\nSimilarly, 56*(65\u221a14 y)/56=65\u221a14 y.\n\nThus, equation becomes:\n\n280x -140x -700 -65\u221a14 y=0.\n\nSimplify:\n\n140x -700 -65\u221a14 y=0 =>140x -65\u221a14 y=700.\n\nDivide through by 35:\n\n4x - (65\u221a14 /35)y=20.\n\nSimplify 65/35=13/7.\n\nThus, 4x - (13\u221a14 /7)y=20.\n\nEquation of tangent at B: 4x - (13\u221a14 /7)y=20.\n\nSimilarly, find equation of tangent at C.\n\nPoint C=(22/5,12\u221a14 /5). Tangent at C: formula is xx1 + yy1 + D(x +x1)/2 + E(y + y1)/2 + F=0.\n\nBut F=0, D=-5, E= -65\u221a14 /28.\n\nThus, tangent at C: x*(22/5) + y*(12\u221a14 /5) + (-5)(x +22/5)/2 + (-65\u221a14 /28)(y +12\u221a14 /5)/2=0.\n\nThis is getting complicated, but let's compute term by term.\n\nFirst term: (22/5)x.\n\nSecond term: (12\u221a14 /5)y.\n\nThird term: (-5)(x +22/5)/2= (-5x -22)/2.\n\nFourth term: (-65\u221a14 /28)(y +12\u221a14 /5)/2= (-65\u221a14 /28)y - (65\u221a14 /28)(12\u221a14 /5)/2.\n\nCompute fourth term:\n\nFirst part: (-65\u221a14 /28)y.\n\nSecond part: (-65\u221a14 /28)*(12\u221a14 /5)/2= (-65*12*(14))/ (28*5*2).\n\nCompute numerator: 65*12*14= 65*168=10920.\n\nDenominator:28*5*2=280.\n\nThus, second part: -10920 /280= -39.\n\nThus, fourth term: (-65\u221a14 /28)y -39.\n\nThus, entire equation:\n\n(22/5)x + (12\u221a14 /5)y + (-5x -22)/2 + (-65\u221a14 /28)y -39=0.\n\nNow, let's combine like terms.\n\nFirst, x terms:\n\n(22/5)x - (5x)/2.\n\nConvert to common denominator, which is 10:\n\n(44/10)x - (25/10)x= (19/10)x.\n\nSecond, y terms:\n\n(12\u221a14 /5)y + (-65\u221a14 /28)y.\n\nConvert to common denominator 140:\n\n(12\u221a14 /5)y= (336\u221a14 /140)y.\n\n(-65\u221a14 /28)y= (-650\u221a14 /140)y.\n\nThus, total y term: (336\u221a14 -650\u221a14)/140 y= (-314\u221a14)/140 y= (-157\u221a14)/70 y.\n\nConstant terms:\n\n-22/2 -39= -11 -39= -50.\n\nThus, equation:\n\n(19/10)x - (157\u221a14)/70 y -50=0.\n\nMultiply through by 70 to eliminate denominators:\n\n19/10 x *70=133x.\n\n-157\u221a14 /70 y *70= -157\u221a14 y.\n\n-50*70= -3500.\n\nThus, equation:\n\n133x -157\u221a14 y -3500=0.\n\nSo, tangent at C:133x -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nNow, we have two tangent equations:\n\nFrom tangent at B:4x - (13\u221a14 /7)y=20.\n\nFrom tangent at C:133x -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nWe need to solve these two equations to find D=(x,y).\n\nLet me write them as:\n\nEquation 1:4x - (13\u221a14 /7)y =20.\n\nEquation 2:133x -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nLet me solve Equation 1 for x:\n\n4x =20 + (13\u221a14 /7)y => x=5 + (13\u221a14 /28)y.\n\nNow, plug into Equation 2:\n\n133*(5 +13\u221a14 /28 y) -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nCompute:\n\n665 + (133*13\u221a14 /28)y -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nSimplify:\n\n665 + (1729\u221a14 /28)y -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nConvert 1729/28=61.5, and 157 is 157/1.\n\nBut let me keep as fractions:\n\n1729/28=61.5, but 1729 \u00f77=247, so 1729/28=247/4.\n\nSimilarly, 157=157/1.\n\nThus:\n\n665 + (247\u221a14 /4)y -157\u221a14 y=3500.\n\nConvert 157\u221a14 y to quarters:157\u221a14 y=628\u221a14 /4 y.\n\nThus:\n\n665 + (247\u221a14 -628\u221a14)/4 y=3500.\n\nSimplify:\n\n665 + (-381\u221a14)/4 y=3500.\n\nThus:\n\n(-381\u221a14)/4 y=3500 -665=2835.\n\nThus:\n\ny=2835 * (-4)/(381\u221a14)= -11340/(381\u221a14).\n\nSimplify:\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 3:\n\n-3790/(127\u221a14).\n\nWait, 2835 \u00f73=945, 381 \u00f73=127.\n\nThus, y= -945/(127\u221a14).\n\nRationalize denominator:\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by \u221a14:\n\ny= -945\u221a14 / (127*14)= -945\u221a14 /1778.\n\nSimplify 945/1778: Divide numerator and denominator by GCD(945,1778).\n\nCompute GCD(945,1778):\n\n1778 \u00f7945=1 with remainder 833.\n\n945 \u00f7833=1 with remainder 112.\n\n833 \u00f7112=7 with remainder 49.\n\n112 \u00f749=2 with remainder 14.\n\n49 \u00f714=3 with remainder 7.\n\n14 \u00f77=2 with remainder 0.\n\nThus, GCD is 7.\n\nThus, 945 \u00f77=135, 1778 \u00f77=254.\n\nThus, y= -135\u221a14 /254.\n\nThus, y= -135\u221a14 /254.\n\nNow, plug y back into Equation 1 to find x.\n\nEquation 1:4x - (13\u221a14 /7)y=20.\n\nThus:\n\n4x=20 + (13\u221a14 /7)*(-135\u221a14 /254).\n\nCompute the second term:\n\n(13\u221a14 /7)*(-135\u221a14 /254)= (13*(-135)*(14))/(7*254).\n\nSimplify:\n\n13*(-135)= -1755.\n\n14/(7)=2.\n\nThus, numerator: -1755*2= -3510.\n\nDenominator:254.\n\nThus, second term: -3510 /254= -3510 \u00f72 /127= -1755 /127.\n\nThus, 4x=20 -1755 /127.\n\nConvert 20 to 2540 /127.\n\nThus, 4x=2540 /127 -1755 /127= (2540 -1755)/127=785 /127.\n\nThus, x=785 / (127*4)=785 /508.\n\nSimplify 785 \u00f7127=6.18. Wait, 127*6=762, 127*6.18\u2248785.\n\nBut exact division:\n\n127*6=762, 785 -762=23.\n\nThus, 785=127*6 +23.\n\nThus, 785/508= (127*6 +23)/508= (127*6)/508 +23/508= (762)/508 +23/508= (762 +23)/508=785/508.\n\nWait, that's same as before.\n\nWait, 785 and508: GCD(785,508).\n\nCompute GCD(508,785):\n\n785 \u00f7508=1 with remainder 277.\n\n508 \u00f7277=1 with remainder 231.\n\n277 \u00f7231=1 with remainder 46.\n\n231 \u00f746=5 with remainder 1.\n\n46 \u00f71=46 with remainder 0.\n\nThus, GCD is1.\n\nThus, x=785/508.\n\nThus, D=(785/508, -135\u221a14 /254).\n\nSimplify coordinates:\n\nx=785/508= (508 +277)/508=1 +277/508.\n\n277 and508: GCD(277,508). 508 \u00f7277=1 with remainder 231. 277 \u00f7231=1 with remainder46. 231 \u00f746=5 with remainder1. 46 \u00f71=46 with remainder0. GCD=1. So x=785/508.\n\nSimilarly, y= -135\u221a14 /254= -135/254\u221a14.\n\nThus, D=(785/508, -135\u221a14 /254).\n\nNow, we need to find AD. Point A is (0,0), so AD is the line from (0,0) to D=(785/508, -135\u221a14 /254).\n\nParametrize AD: any point on AD can be written as t*(785/508, -135\u221a14 /254), where t is a scalar.\n\nWe need to find the other intersection point P of AD with \u03c9.\n\nThus, set parametric equations into circle equation:\n\nx= (785/508)t.\n\ny= (-135\u221a14 /254)t.\n\nPlug into circle equation x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 -5x - (65\u221a14 /28)y=0.\n\nCompute each term:\n\nx\u00b2= (785\u00b2)/(508\u00b2) t\u00b2.\n\ny\u00b2= (135\u00b2*14)/(254\u00b2) t\u00b2.\n\n-5x= -5*(785/508)t.\n\n- (65\u221a14 /28)y= - (65\u221a14 /28)*(-135\u221a14 /254)t= (65*135*14)/(28*254)t.\n\nSimplify:\n\nCompute each term:\n\nFirst, x\u00b2 + y\u00b2:\n\n(785\u00b2)/(508\u00b2) t\u00b2 + (135\u00b2*14)/(254\u00b2) t\u00b2.\n\nSecond, -5x: -5*(785/508)t.\n\nThird, - (65\u221a14 /28)y: positive (65*135*14)/(28*254)t.\n\nCompute the constants:\n\nCompute x\u00b2 + y\u00b2:\n\nCompute (785\u00b2)/(508\u00b2) + (135\u00b2*14)/(254\u00b2).\n\nNote that 254=508/2, so 254\u00b2=508\u00b2/4.\n\nThus, (135\u00b2*14)/(508\u00b2/4)= (135\u00b2*14*4)/508\u00b2= (135\u00b2*56)/508\u00b2.\n\nThus, x\u00b2 + y\u00b2= (785\u00b2 +135\u00b2*56)/508\u00b2 t\u00b2.\n\nCompute 785\u00b2: 785*785. 700\u00b2=490000, 85\u00b2=7225, 2*700*85=119000. So 785\u00b2= (700 +85)\u00b2=700\u00b2 +2*700*85 +85\u00b2=490000 +119000 +7225=490000+119000=609000+7225=616225.\n\nCompute 135\u00b2=18225. 18225*56= let's compute 18225*50=911,250 and 18225*6=109,350. So total=911,250 +109,350=1,020,600.\n\nThus, x\u00b2 + y\u00b2= (616,225 +1,020,600)/508\u00b2 t\u00b2=1,636,825 /508\u00b2 t\u00b2.\n\nCompute -5x: -5*(785/508)t= -3925/508 t.\n\nCompute (65*135*14)/(28*254):\n\n65*135=8,775. 8,775*14=122,650.\n\n28*254=7,112.\n\nThus, 122,650 /7,112= let's divide numerator and denominator by 14:122,650 \u00f714=8,787.5, which is not integer. Alternatively, divide numerator and denominator by 2:61,325 /3,556.\n\nCheck GCD(61325,3556).\n\nCompute 61325 \u00f73556=17.25, not integer. Maybe factor 3556: 3556=4*889. 889 is prime? Let me check: 889 \u00f77=127, yes, 7*127=889.\n\nThus, 3556=4*7*127.\n\nCheck if 61,325 is divisible by 7: 7*8,787=61,309, remainder 16. Not divisible.\n\nThus, fraction is 61,325 /3,556.\n\nThus, (65*135*14)/(28*254)=61,325 /3,556.\n\nThus, equation becomes:\n\n[1,162,600 /508\u00b2] t\u00b2 + [ -5*(785/508) - (61,325 /3,556) ]t +0=0.\n\nWait, this is getting too complicated. Maybe better to use power of point.\n\nPower of point D with respect to \u03c9 is DB\u00b2=DC\u00b2=DA*DP.\n\nBut since D lies outside \u03c9, power of D is equal to DB\u00b2=DC\u00b2=DA*DP.\n\nCompute DB: distance from D to B.\n\nPoint B is (5,0), D is (785/508, -135\u221a14 /254).\n\nCompute DB:\n\nx-coordinate difference:785/508 -5=785/508 -2540/508= (785 -2540)/508= (-1755)/508.\n\ny-coordinate difference: -135\u221a14 /254 -0= -135\u221a14 /254.\n\nThus, DB\u00b2=( (-1755/508)^2 + (-135\u221a14 /254)^2 ).\n\nCompute each term:\n\n(1755)^2= let's compute 1755*1755.\n\nFirst, 1700\u00b2=2,890,000.\n\n55\u00b2=3,025.\n\n2*1700*55=187,500.\n\nThus, 1755\u00b2=2,890,000 +187,500 +3,025=3,080,525.\n\nThus, (1755/508)^2=3,080,525 /508\u00b2.\n\nSimilarly, (135\u221a14 )\u00b2=135\u00b2*14=18,225*14=255,150.\n\nThus, (135\u221a14 /254)^2=255,150 /254\u00b2.\n\nThus, DB\u00b2=3,080,525 /508\u00b2 +255,150 /254\u00b2.\n\nNote that 508=2*254, so 508\u00b2=4*254\u00b2.\n\nThus, DB\u00b2=3,080,525 / (4*254\u00b2) +255,150 /254\u00b2= (3,080,525 +1,020,600)/4*254\u00b2= (4,101,125)/(4*254\u00b2).\n\nSimplify 4,101,125 \u00f725=164,045. 254=2*127, so 254\u00b2=32,516.\n\nThus, DB\u00b2=4,101,125 / (4*32,516)=4,101,125 /129,964\u224831.58.\n\nBut maybe exact fraction.\n\n4,101,125 \u00f725=164,045.\n\n129,964 \u00f74=32,491.\n\nWait, 4,101,125=4,101,125. 129,964=129,964.\n\nNot sure. Maybe leave as is.\n\nThus, power of D is DB\u00b2=4,101,125 /129,964.\n\nThus, DA*DP=DB\u00b2=4,101,125 /129,964.\n\nCompute DA: distance from D to A.\n\nPoint A is (0,0), D is (785/508, -135\u221a14 /254).\n\nThus, DA\u00b2= (785/508)^2 + (135\u221a14 /254)^2.\n\nCompute:\n\n785\u00b2=616,225.\n\n508\u00b2=258,064.\n\n135\u00b2=18,225.\n\n14*18,225=255,150.\n\n254\u00b2=64,516.\n\nThus, DA\u00b2=616,225 /258,064 +255,150 /64,516.\n\nSimplify:\n\nNote that 64,516=4*16,129, and 258,064=4*64,516.\n\nThus, DA\u00b2=616,225/(4*64,516) +255,150 /64,516= (616,225 +1,020,600)/4*64,516=1,636,825 /258,064.\n\nThus, DA= sqrt(1,636,825 /258,064)=sqrt(1,636,825)/508.\n\nCompute sqrt(1,636,825). Let's factor:\n\n1,636,825 \u00f725=65,453. 65,453 \u00f77=9,329. 9,329 \u00f77=1,329. 1,329 \u00f77=189. 189 \u00f77=27.\n\nThus, 1,636,825=25*7^4*27=25*7^4*3^3.\n\nThus, sqrt(1,636,825)=5*7^2*3*sqrt(3)=5*49*3*sqrt(3)=735\u221a3.\n\nThus, DA=735\u221a3 /508.\n\nThus, DA*DP=DB\u00b2=4,101,125 /129,964.\n\nThus, DP= (4,101,125 /129,964)/(735\u221a3 /508)= (4,101,125 /129,964)*(508 /735\u221a3).\n\nSimplify fractions:\n\n4,101,125 \u00f725=164,045.\n\n508 \u00f74=127.\n\n735 \u00f75=147.\n\nThus, DP= (164,045 /51,546)*(127 /147\u221a3).\n\nWait, 4,101,125=25*164,045.\n\n508=4*127.\n\n735=5*147.\n\nThus, DP= (164,045 / (129,964 /25))*(127 / (147\u221a3 /4)).\n\nWait, maybe better to compute:\n\nDP= (4,101,125 *508)/(129,9